  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Saturday)\n\nUpper level ridge continues to be the main weather driver over \nthe weekend with record high temperatures possible through Monday \nafternoon. Monday afternoon a weak upper level trough will push \nthrough Nevada. This trough primarily will help serve as a push to\nupper ridge. There will be a very conditional thunderstorm \nprobability with this trough as it passes through on Monday. With \nthe exception of the NAM, most models show very little upper level\nmoisture making it into interior of Nevada. Observed PWAT values \nfrom OAK and MFR soundings this morning show 0.86\u201d and 0.60\u201d \nrespectively. Which if translated east would be on the low end of \nborderline for precipitation producing storm potential given how \ndry current low levels are. Should PWAT values come in higher than\nforecast, have introduced a low 10% to 20% chance for isolated \nshowers and thunderstorms for northern Nevada Monday afternoon. By\nTuesday the trough will be east into Utah, and into the four \ncorners region, by Wednesday. Upper level ridging forecast to \nbuild back in over the western US, and persist through Friday \nevening. By next Saturday models are still hinting at a pattern \nchange that may bring more active, wetter weather back to Nevada \nin the form of a northern stream upper trough, however confidence \nremains low as there are still large run to run differences in \nplacement and strength of the trough in recent model runs. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in the potential near to record, or \nrecord highs through Monday with high pressure in control.\n\nThere is low confidence for the potential for isolated showers \nfor far northern Nevada Monday afternoon as a weak upper trough \nmoves into Nevada.\n\nThere is high confidence in the return of upper ridging Wednesday\nthrough Friday of Next week. \n\nThere is low confidence for the potential for a pattern change as\na stronger northern stream trough takes aim at Nevada for next \nweekend",
